  "description": "The general election for Oregon's 6th Congressional District, which stretches from the southern Portland suburbs through the Willamette Valley to Salem, features Democratic incumbent Andrea Salinas seeking a third term against Republican nominee David Russ, a former mayor of Dundee. The district, created after the 2020 Census, has a Cook Partisan Voting Index of D+6 and is rated 'Solid D' by the Cook Political Report. Salinas won the open seat in 2022 with 50.0% of the vote and was re-elected in 2024 with 53.4%. Non-affiliated candidate Jason Faler, a combat veteran and healthcare executive, is also seeking ballot access via signature petition and could appear on the November ballot if he meets the required threshold.",
